.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt RMUSER 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm rmuser
.Nd remove users interactively
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl y
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Ar user ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
script removes each
.Ar user ,
or those named in
.Ar file
(whitespace-separated,
.Ql #
starting a comment), or those it asks for if none are named.
For each it shows the account's
.Xr passwd 5
line and asks to confirm, asks whether to remove the home directory,
kills the user's processes, and removes the account with
.Ql pw userdel ,
which also removes its group memberships, its own group, its crontab
and, with the home directory, its mail.
The superuser account
.Ql root
cannot be removed.
It is a simplified
.Fx
.Nm .
It must be run by the superuser.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-f file"
.It Fl f Ar file
Remove the users named in
.Ar file .
.It Fl y
Answer yes to every question.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if a user could not be removed, 64 for a bad command
line, 77 when not run by the superuser.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr adduser 8 ,
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr userdel 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.Fx 2.2 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
